ecognition it has the power to identify  people in real-time photos of large  groups of people and in crowded events  and public places and most notably they  include race as an identifier which  results in increased bias none of these  issues are new in 2016 ProPublica  uncovered bias in the North Point  compass software compass stands for  correctional offender management  profiling for alternative sanctions and  it used it's used by courts to  automatically determine if sentencing  based on criminal recidivism scores that  are set by questions that have extreme  bias against low-income black people so  how do we prevent this kind of  discrimination how do we prevent our  software from ending people's lives we  need to agree on what the ethical  foundation of our work is in this  industry in the workplace and in the  world in 1985 James more detailed in his  essay what is computer ethics these four  tenets it's our responsibility to apply  these tenants to the workplace and ask  these questions when we talk about  machine learning AI and data collection  just to name a few  according to Professor Margaret and  Pearce she defined the fault the need  for the following three ethical  influences an individual personal code  an informal code of ethics and a ethical  conduct or I'm sorry an informal code of  ethics and in code of ethics in the  workplace because unlike our code we  can't say that we were only taking  orders or as Hannah Arden called it  rationalizing in the way of the little  Eichmann's I'd like to remember that  when we talk about ethics the root Greek  word is ethos which translates to habit  or custom and  that is the key to developing an ethical  framework because we need to be  accountable we need to make it a habit  we need to make it a custom in the essay  moral machines by Wendell Wallach and  Colin Allen they wrote about how machine  ethics will drive advancement in human  ethics by forcing us to address gaps in  modern normative theories of et