n he came to  Washington Square Park Jane Jacobs  organized the people of the neighborhood  and put together action like activism to  keep Robert Moses from enacting his plan  Jane Jacobs was really good at the  photo-op she put moms with strollers in  the middle of the park to protest and  she had a ribbon retying ceremony in the  park to mock Robert Moses's  ribbon-cutting ceremonies that he would  do when he opened new highways and  bridges and because she rallied all of  these people and participated in civil  disobedience got arrested for protesting  and at City hearings the mayor was  forced to stop these plans that Robert  Moses had to build a highway through the  middle of the park and what ended up  happening was he went on and he tried to  continue to do this and as he continued  to try to do this in other neighborhoods  tried to carve the middle of Canal  Street down later on in New York City  and Jane Jacobs came back and pushed him  down they kept and got to maintain the  living that they already had they were  able to defend themselves and we  recently saw this happen to in our  industry because yeah just yesterday  Google our Gizmodo reported that Google  will not be pursuing a renewal of their  contract for project maven with the DoD  because of the actions that employees  took over a dozen employees resigned  employees signed paperwork saying that  they did not believe that this was an  ethical decision that they did not want  to participate in dro in writing AI  software for drones and because of this  just like the civil disobedience and the  activism of Jane Jacobs we too can have  an effect on our industry if people  companies are willing to  [Applause]  [Music]  consider how much money companies are  willing to pay to get our attention  how much money they're willing to pay us  in salaries how much money there's  they're spending to sponsor conferences  just like this one we have power over  them as a collective group and we need  to it's our moral imperative to use that  power for good and not for evil and we  need to come up with an ethical  framework to do that that is more  explicit than just good versus evil we  need to decide on codes of ethics the  same way that we decide on codes of  conduct for our conferences codes of  conduct are just ethical codes of ethics  that we apply to our internal group it's  deciding the ways that we want to treat  the people in our society so we need to  apply the same kind of codes to our work  and the world at large it's our job to  design computers to design phones to  design software in a way that no one  dies and to consider the historical  global political social and economic  repercussions of the work that we do so  I want to encourage each and every one  of you to consider the ways that you can  make your work more ethical the ways  that you can prevent people from being  harmed by the software that you write  whether it be through gentrification in  maps whether it be through AI having  bias and machine learning having bias or  even just on your team when your  teammates are the subjective of their  own oppression what are you doing with  your power to help the people who you  work with and the people of the world at  large thank you sir because God will not  have his work made manifest by cowards  you have to be brave you have to take  that responsibility on yourself thank  you  [Applause]
 

